{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/698867-what-are-cthonians","id":698867,"title":"What Are Cthonians?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-12T12:28:43-07:00","id":698867,"title":"What Are Cthonians?","content":"So reading the sourcebook, I'm not sure I understand the concept of Cthonians. Are they supposed to be animals? Predecessor races? Quasi-spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T12:42:13-07:00","id":698890,"title":"","content":"Freaky dead things that were never alive. Natives of the Underworld, or possibly naturalized intruders from emptier parts of reality. Mage's supplement Summoners talks about them in a fair amount of detail, but the gist of it is they're weird things from the Underworld that don't quite approach sapience in a direct fashion and tend to keep to the quieter parts of the Big Black.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T13:53:58-07:00","id":698940,"title":"","content":"I interpret them as the dead and fragmentary remains of things that existed in erased timelines, or the dead remains of lost realities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3081-anachronistic-jam","name":"Anachronistic Jam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T14:49:47-07:00","id":698988,"title":"","content":"For me, Chtonians is a catch-it-all phrase for all kinds of weird sh*t which walks around the Underworld. Dead Old Gods from the Supernal, banished Stygian God Kings, ghosts of races which came before humanity (like dinosaurs), spontaneous creation out of death energy taking form, amalgam of thousands of different ghosts, the ghosts of natural disasters, relics of bygone ages, the native denizens of the Great Below, ancient and mad ghosts, the Neverborn from Wraith, any combination of the above and any other terrifying possibility you can imagine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T07:39:17-07:00","id":699740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/698867-what-are-cthonians?p=698988#post698988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, Chtonians is a catch-it-all phrase for all kinds of weird sh*t which walks around the Underworld. Dead Old Gods from the Supernal, banished Stygian God Kings, ghosts of races which came before humanity (like dinosaurs), spontaneous creation out of death energy taking form, amalgam of thousands of different ghosts, the ghosts of natural disasters, relics of bygone ages, the native denizens of the Great Below, ancient and mad ghosts, the Neverborn from Wraith, any combination of the above and any other terrifying possibility you can imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of that. Most of which is too alien for even Sineaters to sort them into the different things they are.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T10:13:56-07:00","id":701050,"title":"","content":"I would like to see, in a future supplement, Cthonic Sin-Eaters. People who somehow got a Cthonian in them like a Sin-Eater got a Geist. I feel like it could be an interesting sort of mystery Antagonist, and good impetus for Sin-Eaters to try and learn more about the Cthonians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T16:08:47-07:00","id":701378,"title":"","content":"Once I've had a similar ideal of developing the Abmortal sample from the sidebar about a Kereboi bound Sin Eater. Maybe there could be an whole supplement about weird underworld things binding people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T13:30:52-07:00","id":707359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/698867-what-are-cthonians?p=701378#post701378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once I've had a similar ideal of developing the Abmortal sample from the sidebar about a Kereboi bound Sin Eater. Maybe there could be an whole supplement about weird underworld things binding people.</div> </div> </div> </div> Rules as written, the Kerberoi can travel between Dead Dominions to a fair extent, but can't leave the Underworld. It <i>can </i>work as an abnormal phenomenon that challenges the notions that Sin-Eaters have of their purview, however. I recall DaveB saying that Kerberoi in 2e will be Rank 6+ ghosts, so the standard way for one of them to &quot;Bind&quot; themselves to someone would be to create a Royal Avatar in the form of a Rank 5 Geist who shares its personality and general abilities. The Summoners supplement for 1e Mage says that Cthonians can leave the Underworld, but are always in Twilight during their stay. Sin-Eaters who are Bound to a Cthonian probably lack Synergy altogether, and maybe suffer from a persistent Condition that makes ghosts instinctively fear or despise them (if they are even considered Sin-Eaters in-universe).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T00:36:20-08:00","id":817458,"title":"","content":"Summoners says that Cthonians feed on ghosts and are so alien that they don't even register human interactions. but, yeah, making a human/cthonian thin would be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T14:29:52-08:00","id":818738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/698867-what-are-cthonians?p=701378#post701378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once I've had a similar ideal of developing the Abmortal sample from the sidebar about a Kereboi bound Sin Eater. Maybe there could be an whole supplement about weird underworld things binding people.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be an interesting idea; perhaps we could get a minor splat for Geist, like how Ghouls are to Vampire. Being bound to something other than a Geist may come with a number of neat perks, but not all of the ones that a Geist could/would give. I've actually had an idea for a minor splat where instead of being bound to a Geist, the person's soul starts changing into something resembling a Geist, but it's still a work in progress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T04:37:39-08:00","id":819106,"title":"","content":"If it were my Chronicle, I might rule that a number of Chtonians are supernal inhabitants of Stygia that have scuttled through some sort of nether demense or verge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7876-aiwass","name":"Aiwass","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}